      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R1"],
      "pins": ["R1.1", "R1.2", "Q1.2", "J1.3"],
      "nets": ["R1 current-sense node (Q1 source / J1.3 RESE / GND)"],
      "observed": "On sheet /EPD_Driver/, R1 (the boost-converter current-sense resistor in the Q1 source path feeding J1.3 'RESE') carries the value '0.47mohm' (0.47 milliohm).",
      "expected": "The specification states R1 = 0.47 Ω ('R1 | 0.47 Ω current-sense resistor' and 'R1 default (G1/G2 group): 0.47 Ω | R1 = 0.47 Ω | Matches G1, G2 default (0.47 Ω)'). 0.47 mΩ is three orders of magnitude too small.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R1 / 0.47mohm (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, between Q1 source and the J1.3/RESE–GND node)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "R1 | 0.47 Ω current-sense resistor | EPD booster current-limit sense"}
      ],
      "impact": "The voltage developed across the sense resistor at the panel's operating current would be ~1000× too small, so the EPD COG's booster control loop (RESE feedback) would read near-zero current, fail to regulate, and likely overdrive/overcurrent the boost stage (consistent with the documented Q1 heating symptom) or fail to generate the EPD drive voltages.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch / boost-converter input"],
      "observed": "On sheet /EPD_Driver/, C1 (the bulk input capacitor at the L1/Display_Power_Switch node, in parallel with C2) is drawn as '0.1uF/16V'.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table maps the PDI default capacitor to 'C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V', i.e. C1 should be 1 µF/25 V, not 0.1 µF/16 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 / 0.1uF/16V (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, Display_Power_Switch node to GND)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "A 10× smaller input capacitor at the boost-converter input raises input ripple and reduces the energy reservoir for the EPD charge pump, degrading boost regulation; the 16 V rating is also below the 25 V the reference specifies.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the reference in the EPD_Driver sheet: R1, the boost current-sense resistor, is valued '0.47mohm' instead of the specified 0.47 Ω (a 1000× error that breaks the panel's booster current feedback), and C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V. Other documented quirks (unconnected RJ45 data pads, bit-banged EPD SPI pins, barrel-jack battery disconnect, S1 as reset) match the specification and are not reported."
}

